    rdf:value """Thursday, Dec. 5, 1907
Rainy.
Algar.
Worked.
Mr. J. H. Breck came to lunch, a feeble, unimportant pupil of Denman Ross.
Craig sent up his etchings, asking B.B. to write a preface. We had to take them 400 francs. B.B. does not particularly like them."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 361 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1907> .

